WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:16.240
Jon Snow was originally supposed to kill the
Night King on Game of Thrones.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.960
Arya Stark killed the Night King in the final
season of Game of Thrones during the battle

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.050
for Winterfell,
but according to the cast, it wasn’t always

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.470
supposed to go that way.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.469
A few days ago Maisie Williams (an actress
who played Arya Stark) revealed that Kit Harington

00:00:29.469 --> 00:00:32.250
(an actor who plays Jon Snow) told her and
everyone else

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.610
that he was going to go that way, quoting
Kit

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.670
''Someone told me in season 3 that I was going
to kill The Night King.”And this is what

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.989
should have happened.

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:43.530
That would have given us a satisfying conclusion
to Jon Snow's story.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.780
That would have fulfilled the long built prophecy
of Jon Snow being the Prince that was promised.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.399
That would have justified Rhaegar and his
obsession with prophecies as well,

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:56.190
especially because creating Jon Snow who Rhaegar
believed would be the Prince that was promised,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:00.539
it cost Rhaegar his own life as well as the
lives of his both wives,

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:04.830
Lyanna who died giving birth to Jon and Rhaegar’s
first wife Ellia.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.130
Children Rhaegar had with Elia were also brutally
killed.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:12.450
The Mad King died as well as 10s of thousands
of soldiers on both sides.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.080
All these deaths, the end of the long Targaryen
dynasty just because Rhaegar thought Jon had

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.800
to be created, only for all of it, including
Jon's true heritage to not be important at

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.210
all at the end.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.250
Jon killing the Night King would have justified
why Jon Snow was brought back to life.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.980
It would have justified all the build-up to
this epic fight between the Night King and

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.900
Jon Snow
that’s been building for years.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.340
All of that to be for nothing,
just because the showrunners David Benioff

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.780
and Dan Weiss decided it would be too obvious
for Jon to kill the Night King which was the

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.800
original plan and changed it to be Arya.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.610
Don't be fooled by thinking Arya was planned
to kill the Night King all along,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.390
and don't think it was foreshadowed to happen
way back in season 3 when Melisandre made

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:56.500
a prophecy to her about shutting the blue
eyes among the others, that she would repeat

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.500
to her in season 8 before she kills the Night
King.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.620
That Arya-Melisandre scene where Melisandre
reminds her of the eyes she would shut forever,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.759
and how the blue eyes are the only left from
the prophecy, well it wasn’t foreshadowing

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:09.759
anything.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:14.080
Yes, Arya did kill the Night King who has
blue eyes, but at the time Melisandre first

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.170
made this prophecy to Arya, as I already mentioned,
it was back in season 3, in 2013.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.459
Do you know when the showrunners decided it
would be Arya who kills the Night King?

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:24.600
In 2016!

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.069
After season 8 episode 3, the battle for Winterfell
aired,

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:31.450
the showrunners revealed that they made a
decision 3 years ago

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.140
that it would be Arya to kill the leader of
the White Walkers.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:39.549
This was in 2019 which means David Benioff
and Dan Weiss decided around 2016,

00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:43.040
after season 6 was made that it would be Arya
who kills the Night King.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.040
This confirms Melisandre’s prophecy had
nothing to do with the Night King

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.650
as this scene took place in 2013 and it was
3 years after this scene

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.749
that the showrunners switched from Jon to
Arya to kill the Night King.

00:02:53.749 --> 00:02:58.030
Arya’s whole story was about vengeance,
and her years of training with the Faceless

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.750
Men were justified when she avenged the killing
of her family when she avenged the Red Wedding

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.260
by using faces to kill Walder Frey.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.859
She could have also used those faces to kill
Cersei, and once again avenge her family.

00:03:09.859 --> 00:03:12.790
That was her story, not the White Walkers
and not the Night King.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.680
They were Jon Snow’s story since Season
1.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.760
Arya killing the Night King makes as much
sense as if Jon Snow ended up killing Walder

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.140
Frey or Cersei because that simply isn’t
what his story was built up to.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.450
When the word of his father’s Ned Stark’s
fate reaches the Wall,

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.489
Jon initially wants to ride south and join
Robb in vengeance for his father,

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:35.859
but he doesn’t because Lord Commander Jeor
Mormont convinces him that those wars and

00:03:35.859 --> 00:03:39.549
the game of thrones are not important
because there is only one war that matters

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:41.590
and it’s against the White Walkers.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.200
Arya did not have anything to do with the
White Walker story,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.969
she didn’t know they existed until the very
final season

00:03:46.969 --> 00:03:51.120
while Jon’s whole story on the other hand
was about the White Walkers and the great

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.510
war that was coming.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:57.290
In season 1 episode 1 Jon Snow is with his
father when a deserter of the Night's Watch

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.720
is brought before Ned to be executed.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.969
That deserter named Will who ran away after
seeing the White Walkers kill his fellow brothers

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:07.669
of the Night's Watch, tells them what he saw,
the White Walkers.

00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:11.510
Ned executes him because that is the law for
abandoning the Night's Watch.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.840
So Jon is involved in the whole story since
the very beginning.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.449
During season 1, he's a man to kill the first
wight in a thousands of years

00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:23.610
when the corpse brought back to the Wall becomes
wight and attacks Lord Commander Mormont.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:28.870
Jon saves Mormont's life by burning a wight,
earning a pardon for his earlier misdemeanor

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.310
as well as Valyrian steel sword Longclaw.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.700
In season 2 Jon's story continues to be about
the threat beyond the Wall

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.620
as they ride north of the wall seeking for
Benjen and an explanation for the wight attack.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.200
Jon sees Craster carrying a newborn into the
woods, leaving the child for a White Walker

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.200
as a sacrifice.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.250
In season 3, Jon and the Free Folk arrive
at the Fist of the First Men,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.200
only to survey the bloody aftermath of the
assault on the Night's Watch by the White

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.500
Walkers
and their army of wights.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.160
In season 4, Jon takes a little break from
the White Walker story due to the threat of

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.840
the wildlings, but he's still very much aware
that they are out there,

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.790
advising Stannis to burn the bodies of the
dead wildlings in order to prevent them from

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.290
returning as wights.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.500
In season 5, the White Walker story gets him
killed.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.950
Jon makes a hard choice and does what he believes
is the best

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:19.250
and that is rescuing the Free Folk from Hardhome
and allowing them to pass the Wall

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.340
and settle in the North to keep them from
falling into the hands of the coming White

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.060
Walker army
as he knows that if they stay out there, they

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.000
would be killed, then resurrected
and added to the ever-growing army of the

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.000
undead.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.700
While doing so, Hardhome is attacked by the
Night King's army

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.720
and Jon fights the White Walker and kills
him with Longclaw.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.390
The Night King watches Jon intensely with
interest from a distance.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.120
The Night King and Jon share a long glance
with each other

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.580
as the Night King uses his magic to raise
all of the dead as wights before Jon's eyes.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.860
Still, Jon saved some of the Free Folk from
dying and joining the White Walker army

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.080
and allowed them to go south of the Wall,
which got him killed.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.960
In season 6 Jon is resurrected by Melisandre
and the Lord of Light

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.690
because he still has a role to play in the
great war.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.930
In the aftermath of his victory at Winterfell
and the confirmation from the Citadel that

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:09.370
winter has come,
Jon Snow warns the gathered lords of the North

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:14.090
and the Vale who wish to return home that
the war is not over, alluding at the coming

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.340
of the Night King.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.520
In season 7 Jon prepares the North for the
upcoming great war against the White Walkers.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:25.170
Upon receiving 2 letters, one an invitation
from Tyrion to come and meet Daenerys at Dragonstone,

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.800
and the second from Sam informing him of his
discovery of dragon glass on Dragonstone,

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.611
Jon decides to go to Dragonstone, risk his
life because that's the only chance for the

00:06:34.611 --> 00:06:36.140
North to win this war.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:39.860
Jon leads a mission to capture a wight and
prove to Cersei that the threat is real

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:44.340
in hopes to put a stop on fighting among the
living and get the support of the Lannister

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.670
army as well.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:49.860
Jon fights a White Walker again, kills a bunch
of wights, and once again shares a glance

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.250
with the Night King.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.960
Not once, but 2 times.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.740
As you can see, the White Walkers were the
core of Jon's story, they were his purpose

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.020
and his destiny.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.800
And few days ago it’s confirmed that Jon
Snow was originally supposed to be the one

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:06.270
to kill the Night King, as it's revealed Kit
said they told him in season 3 it would be

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:10.950
his character Jon Snow killing the Night King
which makes complete sense.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.260
The Night King’s actor was changed because
they planned to have the Night King vs Jon

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:20.170
Snow epic fight where Jon Snow prevails, hence
why they switched from an actual actor playing

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.640
the Night King
to one of the world's best swordsman and 33

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.720
years experienced stunt man.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:30.210
All of this buildup for years and years was
destroyed when in 2016 after the release of

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.790
season 6,
the showrunners decided that they left way

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.920
too many clues of Jon being the one to kill
the Night King, and instead of giving us a

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.000
satisfying conclusion to Jon's story and have
him kill the Night King,

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.420
the showrunners changed it to Arya and went
for a shock value instead.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.520
Their explanation on why they decided for
it to be Arya who kills the Night King,

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:55.030
instead of Jon who's entire story from season
1 -- up until season 8 was building for this

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:59.760
great showdown between him and the Night King,
which was supposed to fulfill his destiny,

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.600
wrap up his story perfectly:
Benioff said “we hoped to kind of avoid

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.930
the expected, and Jon Snow has always been
the hero,

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:11.220
the one who’s been the savior, but it just
didn’t seem right to us, for this moment.”

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.290
Jon was literally made for this moment -- while
its Arya's first time seeing White Walkers

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.010
and wights and the Night King.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.040
You can't make all that build up and throw
it away

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.690
just because you want to avoid the expected.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.320
Good writing should be more valued than the
shock value.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.700
I'm going to leave the last words to none
other than George RR Martin

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.790
who perfectly explained why changing the story
plot just because people expect it's not a

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:35.289
good choice as it takes away the satisfaction
of the build-up,

00:08:35.289 --> 00:09:04.630
makes all the planted clues and foreshadows
a dead end and ultimately ruins everything:

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:47.570
Thank you 

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.960
guys so much for watching, I hope you enjoyed
this video

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:53.690
and if you did please give it a big thumbs
up and I hope to see you in the next one!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:53.980
Peace

